soak-test: started 4 groups of one responder, 3 callers, 1 grinder and 1 tick waiter (24 user threads) on 4 online core(s), beating every 5s
soak-test: silence longer than a few beats is a hang, not a slow run; the beat is on the wall clock and does not depend on the workload making progress
soak-test: a clean run is a number to compare against, NOT evidence that the concurrency is correct (design/roadmap/0219-a-workload-that-does-not-stop.md)
soak-test: the threads that cross cores are the tick waiters, NOT the rendezvous pairs; a rising crossings count is the wake protocol sustained across cores under load, not the IPC workload migrating (design/roadmap/0221-a-soak-that-crosses-cores.md)
soak-test: rounds counts IPC round trips and wakes counts tick-route wakes; they are separate because they are separate quantities, and neither rate compares with a soak built differently
soak-test-census: where the kernel placed each worker at spawn: R=responder, C=caller, G=grinder, W=tick waiter, and the number after each letter is its group
soak-test-census: core=0 threads=6 R0 W0 C1 C2 C2 C3
soak-test-census: core=2 threads=5 G0 C1 C1 G2 C3
soak-test-census: core=4 threads=6 C0 C0 W1 W2 C3 G3
soak-test-census: core=6 threads=7 C0 R1 G1 R2 C2 R3 W3
soak-test-census: this is the boot-time lottery and NOT where the run settles: a rendezvous wake queues the peer on the waker's own core (DECISIONS 138, how a saturated workload is made to hand threads across cores), so each group converges onto one core within a few exchanges
soak-test-census: the beat line's drifted= is how many responders, callers and grinders are no longer on the core the census above put them on; while it reads 0 that census is current, and a nonzero one is followed by the census that replaces it
soak-test-census: tick waiters are excluded from drifted= because their movement is the point rather than a surprise, and it is already crossings= (design/roadmap/0221-a-soak-that-crosses-cores.md)
soak-test-watchdog: found the Intel TCO watchdog: Pch layout, TCO registers at I/O port 0x400
soak-test-watchdog: the previous boot was not ended by this watchdog (SECOND_TO_STS clear)
soak-test-watchdog: ARMED. THIS BUILD RESETS THE MACHINE IF THE SOAK STOPS BEATING: 50 ticks of 0.6s counted twice, so a reset 60.0s after the last pet, which comes every 5s from the beat.
soak-test-watchdog: a soak that FAILS prints its verdict and dump and then stops petting, so the reset follows the evidence and never replaces it. To stop the watchdog: press any key on this console. It is halted at the next beat and the soak keeps running.
